SUMMARY:Art Break | Dawn Roe
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an informal gallery talk with contemporary photographer\, Dawn Roe\, who will guide us through Poetic Exposures\, photographs from the Collection. \nRoe\, who has three of her works featured in the exhibition\, will share her unique perspective on the history of photography and her own practice. \nDawn Roe’s work has been exhibited throughout the U.S. and internationally. The recipient of honors and grants as well as numerous artist residencies\, her imagery and writing has been featured in many print and on-line publications. Roe received a BFA from Marylhurst University and an MFA from Illinois State University. She divides her time between Asheville and Winter Park\, Florida where she serves as Professor of Art at Rollins College.  \n\nRESERVE TICKETS NOW
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/art-break-dawn-roe/
LOCATION:Asheville Art Museum\, 2 South Pack Square\, Asheville\, NC\, 28801\, United States
CATEGORIES:Art Break
