SUMMARY:South Arts: Southern Circuit Tour of Independent Filmmakers | Minnie Evans: Draw or Die
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a screening of Minnie Evans: Draw or Die followed by a conversation with the filmmaker\, Linda Royal. \nWe are also excited that Wayne Evans\, the great-grandson of Minnie Evans\, who is in the documentary\, will be attending the Q&A as well. \nSouthern Circuit screenings are funded in part by a grant from South Arts\, a regional arts organization\, in partnership with the National Endowment for the Arts. For more information about Southern Circuit please visit www.southarts.org/southerncircuit. \nScreening time: 56:10:00 \nFilm Synopsis: \nThe film explores the inspirational life and artistic mastery of visionary artist Minnie Evans through archived\nconversations with her friend Nina Howell Starr. \nAbout the filmmaker: \nLinda Royal (fka Linda Booker) directed\, produced\, and edited the film festival award-winning\ndocumentaries “STRAWS\,” with narration by Tim Robbins\, “Bringing It Home\,” and “Love Lived on Death\nRow.” Her films have reached audiences worldwide through film festivals\, educational distribution\,\ncommunity screenings\, corporate offices\, and in-flight entertainment. She has partnered with numerous\norganizations for grassroots advocacy and impact campaigns. Linda was the Director of Operations for\nthe Sonoma International Film Festival in 2015-2016. She started By the Brook Productions after receiving\na Certificate in Documentary Studies from Duke University in 2005. Before filmmaking\, Linda was an Art\nDirector and graphic designer for numerous publications in Florida and North Carolina. \n  \nLimited Capacity \nRESERVE TICKETS NOW \nhttps://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/minnie_evans__draw_or_die_trailer_2_min.-240p.mp4
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/south-arts-film-talk-minnie-evans-draw-or-die/
LOCATION:Asheville Art Museum\, 2 South Pack Square\, Asheville\, NC\, 28801\, United States
CATEGORIES:In Conversation,South Arts Film Circuit
